WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.091
Pinocchio ate breakfast quickly.

2
00:00:03.092 --> 00:00:07.883
He was very hungry, but he was also in a hurry to see Geppetto.

3
00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:16.809
He thanked the farmer and ran from the house, across the field, and back to the road where his troubles had started.

4
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:21.337
As Pinocchio walked, he saw familiar places along the road.

5
00:00:21.338 --> 00:00:25.472
"Look, there is the Field of Follies," he exclaimed.

6
00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:32.157
A few hours later, he said, "Look, that is where I met Mr. Fox and Mr. Cat."

7
00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:36.323
He tried not to cry about his foolish mistake.

8
00:00:36.324 --> 00:00:43.932
After a few more hours, he said, "Look, that is where I escaped from the marionette master!

9
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:47.116
Oh, what an adventure I have had.

10
00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:50.861
But it is taking too long to walk home.

11
00:00:50.862 --> 00:00:57.434
I have walked almost all day, and I’m still so far away."

12
00:00:57.435 --> 00:01:00.820
Pinocchio sat on a log and started to cry.

13
00:01:00.821 --> 00:01:03.557
He was tired and he missed Geppetto.

14
00:01:03.558 --> 00:01:10.897
As he cried, he could hear a soft voice calling his name: "Pinocchio . . . Pinocchio."

15
00:01:10.898 --> 00:01:18.185
"I am here!" Pinocchio shouted, looking around to see who the voice belonged to.

16
00:01:18.186 --> 00:01:22.894
Suddenly, there was a loud whoosh and a lot of feathers.

17
00:01:22.895 --> 00:01:25.484
"Ah, there you are!

18
00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:30.294
I have been looking for you all month," said a handsome eagle.

19
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:32.365
"You were looking for me?

20
00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:35.476
How did you know my name?"

21
00:01:35.477 --> 00:01:39.514
"Ah, I am an old friend of Geppetto.

22
00:01:39.515 --> 00:01:43.236
He saved me when I was a little egg.

23
00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.413
When I heard he had lost his boy, I wanted to help.

24
00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:51.344
So, I have been flying everywhere calling your name.

25
00:01:51.345 --> 00:01:55.198
I am so happy to find you!"

26
00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:58.075
Pinocchio began to jump and dance.

27
00:01:58.076 --> 00:01:59.761
"You know Geppetto!

28
00:01:59.762 --> 00:02:01.759
Oh, that’s wonderful!

29
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.333
I will see my father soon!"

30
00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:08.600
"Well, not as soon as you may think," said the eagle.

31
00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:12.519
"Why not?" asked Pinocchio, worried.

32
00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.178
"When you did not come home from school, Geppetto searched the woods.

33
00:02:17.179 --> 00:02:19.665
Then, he searched the countryside.

34
00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:22.253
Then, he searched all of Italy.

35
00:02:22.254 --> 00:02:29.202
After searching for a month, he has decided to sail to Sicily and Sardinia to find you.

36
00:02:29.203 --> 00:02:33.591
So he built a boat and will sail away today."

37
00:02:33.592 --> 00:02:38.252
"Oh no! If only I could get there quickly.

38
00:02:38.253 --> 00:02:42.366
Mr. Eagle, could you please help me find my father?"

39
00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:47.526
"Of course! I’m happy to help a friend," he answered.

40
00:02:47.527 --> 00:02:52.419
The eagle carefully grabbed Pinocchio with his claws and flew into the sky.

41
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:59.944
Below him, Pinocchio could see the forest, the countryside, and the sea.

42
00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:05.996
In only a few flaps of the eagle’s wings, Pinocchio could see the beach and a crowd of people.

43
00:03:05.997 --> 00:03:09.460
"Please drop me there," he said, pointing.

44
00:03:09.461 --> 00:03:16.051
The eagle carefully set Pinocchio in the sand and flew away, calling, "Good luck, Pinocchio."

45
00:03:16.052 --> 00:03:21.720
"Thank you!" Pinocchio called back.

46
00:03:21.721 --> 00:03:25.166
Pinocchio ran through the crowd, looking for Geppetto.

47
00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:29.136
"Excuse me, where is Geppetto?" he said.

48
00:03:29.137 --> 00:03:32.755
"Who is Geppetto?" a bystander asked.

49
00:03:32.756 --> 00:03:34.781
"Geppetto is my father.

50
00:03:34.782 --> 00:03:38.782
He has gray hair and a kind smile."

51
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:41.131
The bystander looked sad.

52
00:03:41.132 --> 00:03:45.130
"Oh, I am terribly sorry, little boy.

53
00:03:45.131 --> 00:03:48.435
Do you see that small boat out there?

54
00:03:48.436 --> 00:03:50.441
That is Geppetto."

55
00:03:50.442 --> 00:03:55.786
Pinocchio looked out at the waves and could see a small brown dot.

56
00:03:55.787 --> 00:04:00.923
"Oh no! He is so far away," Pinocchio said.

57
00:04:00.924 --> 00:04:02.833
"Oh, look at the sky!

58
00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:06.487
It is going to rain soon and Father could drown.

59
00:04:06.488 --> 00:04:09.014
I must help him."

60
00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:13.998
Before anyone could stop him, Pinocchio dived into the ocean.

61
00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:21.778
He began the long swim toward Geppetto’s boat.

